WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.180
Let's take a quick look at how to create
custom Compute Engine instances.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.880
Open your Google Cloud dashboard and go to
the Compute Engine section.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:14.580
Now click create instance. Here, you can see the
customized link you can customize the

00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:18.890
number of CPU cores as well as the
gigabytes of memory for your instance

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.440
once you've selected all the appropriate
options scroll down and click create.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:26.780
in a few seconds your custom VM should be
created

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.140
you can also create a custom VM using
the gcloud tool.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:41.579
Run 'gcloud compute instances create' then give it the name of your new instance, and now you can use

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:47.010
the --custom-cpu flag followed
by the number of CPU course and the

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:52.100
--custom-memory flag followed by the
gigabytes of memory. In a few seconds you

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.309
can see your new VM!

